\par Before you create an application window, you must register a window class
\par by calling RegisterClass. This function requires a single parameter. What is
\par that parameter and how will be the syntax of the structure?
\par Answwer:
\par The function requires a structure of type WNDClass as parameter. This
\par structure includes two fields that are pointers to character strings, so the
\par structure is defined two different ways in the WINUSER.H header file. First,
\par there's the ASCII version, WNDCLASSA:
\par typedef struct tagWNDCLASSA
\par \{ 
\par UINT style ;
\par WNDPROC lpfnWndProc ;
\par int cbClsExtra ;
\par int cbWndExtra ;
\par HINSTANCE hInstance ;
\par HICON hIcon ;
\par HCURSOR hCursor ;
\par HBRUSH hbrBackground ;
\par LPCSTR lpszMenuName ;
\par 
\par }\pard \qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\intbl\faauto\rin0\lin0 {\b\insrsid5067159 Page 69}{\insrsid5067159 \cell }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {\insrsid5067159 \trowd \irow0\irowband0\lastrow 
